// spec: 12 Runtime panics; stdlib Time
// addDuration sums exact units and days, balancing up to the larger of the largest units, and
// is a panic on years, months or weeks, whose length it cannot know.
Time.addDuration(Time.duration(minutes: 90), Time.duration(minutes: 30)) // => PT120M
Time.addDuration(Time.duration(days: 1), Time.duration(hours: 25)) // => P2DT1H
Time.addDuration(Time.duration(months: 1), Time.duration(hours: 1)) // => panic: Time.addDuration: years, months and weeks cannot be added without a starting point; add each to a date

// A date that is not there is a panic, as a constructor rejects what with constrains.
Time.plainDate(2024, 2, 29)                   // => 2024-02-29
Time.plainDate(2026, 2, 30)                   // => panic: Time.plainDate: no such date: 2026-02-30

// A time field out of range is a panic.
Time.plainTime(23, 59, 59, 999, 999, 999)     // => 23:59:59.999999999
Time.plainTime(25)                            // => panic: Time.plainTime: hour out of range: 25

// compareDuration orders by length, and is a panic on years, months or weeks without a
// relativeTo point to measure them from.
Time.compareDuration(Time.duration(hours: 1), Time.duration(minutes: 90)) // => -1
Time.compareDuration(Time.duration(months: 1), Time.duration(days: 30), relativeTo: Time.plainDate(2026, 2, 1)) // => -1
Time.compareDuration(Time.duration(months: 1), Time.duration(days: 30)) // => panic: Time.compareDuration: years, months or weeks need a relativeTo point to compare

// A day added to an instant is a panic: an instant has no calendar.
Time.add(Time.fromEpochMillis(0), Time.duration(hours: 24)) // => 1970-01-02T00:00:00Z
Time.add(Time.fromEpochMillis(0), Time.duration(days: 1)) // => panic: Time.add: an instant has no calendar; days cannot be added to it

// fromEpochMillis is a panic beyond 100 million days from the epoch.
Time.fromEpochMillis(8640000000000000)        // => +275760-09-13T00:00:00Z
Time.fromEpochMillis(8640000000000001)        // => panic: Time.fromEpochMillis: outside the range of time values

// A duration with fields of both signs is a panic.
Time.duration(hours: -1, minutes: -30)        // => -PT1H30M
Time.duration(hours: 1, minutes: -1)          // => panic: Time.duration: a duration's fields must all have one sign

// epochNanos is a panic outside 1677 to 2262, where the nanoseconds do not fit an int.
var last = Result.unwrap(Time.parseInstant("2262-04-11T23:47:16.854775807Z"))
Time.epochNanos(last)                         // => 9223372036854775807
var far = Result.unwrap(Time.parseInstant("2300-01-01T00:00:00Z"))
Time.epochNanos(far)                          // => panic: Time.epochNanos: the nanoseconds do not fit an int; the instant is outside 1677 to 2262

// Rounding a date-time to a calendar unit is a panic, as is an increment that does not fit.
var dt = Result.unwrap(Time.parsePlainDateTime("2021-07-01T12:34:56"))
Time.round(dt, Time.Hour{}, 6)                // => 2021-07-01T12:00:00
Time.round(dt, Time.Month{})                  // => panic: Time.round: months cannot be rounded to
Time.round(dt, Time.Hour{}, 7)                // => panic: Time.round: the increment for hours must divide 24 and be smaller, not 7

// roundDuration balances to largestUnit or rounds to smallestUnit, and with neither given has
// nothing to do, which is a panic.
Time.roundDuration(Time.duration(minutes: 90), largestUnit: Time.Hour{}) // => PT1H30M
Time.roundDuration(Time.duration(minutes: 90)) // => panic: Time.roundDuration: roundDuration needs a smallest or a largest unit

// since takes the units its type has and is a panic on one it lacks, as until is: a
// PlainTime has no days.
var a = Time.plainTime(10, 30)
var b = Time.plainTime(9, 0)
Time.since(a, b)                              // => PT1H30M
Time.since(a, b, Time.Day{})                  // => panic: Time.since: a time has no days

// A total of months without a relativeTo point is a panic.
Time.total(Time.duration(days: 2), Time.Hour{}) // => 48.0
Time.total(Time.duration(months: 1), Time.Day{}) // => panic: Time.total: a total with months needs a relativeTo point

// with constrains a field the type has and is a panic on a field it lacks: a PlainDate has
// no hour.
Time.with(Time.plainDate(2026, 1, 31), month: 2) // => 2026-02-28
Time.with(Time.plainDate(2026, 1, 31), hour: 1) // => panic: Time.with: a date has no time fields

// A year so large that its day count overflows is a panic, not a date.
Time.plainDate(3989932118587117601, 3, 1)     // => panic: Time.plainDate: outside the range of time values
